text:
Mia Wang: Quick q  compact left nav + deep links: keep a breadcrumb or drop it and rely on header context? noticed workspace filter sometimes disappears when using short links :thinking_face:
Jamie Lee: short answer: keep a slim breadcrumb for context. Users landing from emails expect to see where they ended up. If we hide it, header must always show workspace name and be focusable for a11y.
Omar Khan: Routing note: we should pick a canonical path (`/w/:ws/...`) and rewrite `/models/:id?ws=` to that on first load. That makes hydration deterministic and analytics cleaner.
Nora Patel: Accessibility: condensed crumbs must include `nav` landmark, each crumb needs aria-current="page" when active, and truncated crumbs need `aria-label` with full text. For mobile, tap should open an accessible sheet (role=dialog) with actions.
Mia Wang: UX: condensed row = single line, smaller type, ellipsize workspace. On mobile small widths we hide workspace label and surface it in the sheet. Tooltip OK on desktop, not on mobile.
navbot: Spec updated: https://redwood.design/ux/nav-mini-breadcrumbs  includes canary schedule and a11y checklist.
Jamie Lee: Quick hydration snippet for router (very small):
```
// run once on app boot
if (location.search.includes('ws=') && location.pathname.startsWith('/models/')) {
  const params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
  const ws = params.get('ws');
  const id = location.pathname.split('/').pop();
  history.replaceState({}, '', `/w/${ws}/models/${id}` + location.search);
  telemetry.track('rewrite_ws_query');
}
```
Omar Khan: Also migrate old hash `#panel=` -> `?panel=` and emit `legacy_hash_migration` event. Avoid encoding UI-only state in path segments; use query params for ephemeral panels.
Nora Patel: Microcopy: in mobile sheet use "Open parent workspace" and label the breadcrumb toggle "Show path" for screen readers. Also ensure 4.5:1 contrast on focus outline for crumbs.
Mia Wang: I'll update mocks and post new frames here. Thanks! :raised_hands:
